 17592186288390 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288391 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288392 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288393 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288394 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1041 "selection" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288393 13194139534441 true] [17592186288389 1110 #uuid "ef91dae4-9dde-5751-9c5f-7995f46057bf" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288390 1034 "x-5=-6t,\\,\\,y+2=-3{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288390 1111 #uuid "8e0eb2be-bc36-5cad-b102-f63bde897b30" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288391 1034 "x-2=-{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=-2t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288391 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288391 1111 #uuid "6cd55ad8-4124-5733-9f0a-59af107645f3" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288392 1034 "x+2=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=-6t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288392 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288392 1111 #uuid "83b5fd85-0f2d-57e9-a0c2-c598ef02e598" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288393 1034 "x-2=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=-6t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288393 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288393 1111 #uuid "70dc7a8d-0093-57c2-bb9c-4a6b44a79748" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288394 1034 "x-5=-3{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+2=-6t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288394 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288394 1111 #uuid "e0485994-9768-54ef-a94e-b9fc4f91eed2" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288396 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1089 "q-106465" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1100 "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y+1)^{2}=-(x-3)?$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1113 #uuid "efd48b95-db5f-52c0-99e2-d4c8610ebe36" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288395 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(3,-1).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx-3=p{t}^{2},\\,y+1=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =-(x-3) \\\\ 4p(x-3) & =-(x-3) \\\\ 4p & =-1 \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-3=(-\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\\,y+1=2(-\\frac{1}{4})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t.\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288397 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288398 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288399 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288400 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288401 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1041 "selection" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288400 13194139534441 true] [17592186288396 1110 #uuid "a9bd091d-91d9-5843-968d-693b832cddd7" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288397 1034 "x-3=-4{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-8t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288397 1111 #uuid "8823679c-4206-593e-9924-bba1b808b386" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288398 1034 "x-3=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288398 1111 #uuid "9445efe6-ebcf-5fed-8a56-5ce164ddda33" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288399 1034 "x+3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288399 1111 #uuid "b8ce72c8-fabe-53b4-9353-dea6391c44b9" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288400 1034 "x-3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288400 1111 #uuid "9f933ccb-75fa-51e5-b46c-a9bcbb9b8b57" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288401 1034 "x-1=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+3=-\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288401 1111 #uuid "32999de3-d390-5e7b-8e44-6029adc7ac8f" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288403 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1089 "q-106503" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx+2=-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y+3=-\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1113 #uuid "90e7bbda-fedf-5ef5-9757-a13f2517bec7" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288402 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-2(x+2),\\,{t}^{2}=-4(y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-2(x+2))}^{2} \\\\  & =4{(x+2)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-4(y+3)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x+2)}^{2} & =-4(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =-(y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288403 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288404 1319