y+1=-\\frac{4}{25}\\,{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534441 true] [17592186288409 1113 #uuid "4eca1d59-0a7a-514c-be56-d9295bc3b025" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288409 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{5}{2}(x-4),\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{5}{2}(x-4))}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\,(x-4)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{25}{4}\\,(x-4)^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{4}(y+1) \\\\ {(x-4)}^{2} & =-(y+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288411 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288412 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1041 "field-1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288411 13194139534441 true] [17592186288410 1110 #uuid "430e6a32-c5ac-536e-895d-3f04d1aa6890" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288411 1034 "4" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288411 1111 #uuid "b7a9c3fe-b99a-57ac-b2b3-147b483ebeab" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288412 1034 "5" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288412 1111 #uuid "c1f56675-0ca9-546d-8c77-52d997de7ead" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288414 13194139534441 true] [17592186288413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288413 1041 "field-2" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288414 13194139534441 true] [17592186288413 1110 #uuid "1bb41120-1a14-5ab8-8ea6-dbbc84a01976" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288414 1034 "-y-1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288414 1111 #uuid "dbec2081-f15a-5ba0-aa49-e407ae6eddb1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288416 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288418 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1089 "q-323216" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y-3=5t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,-$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1113 #uuid "63957822-af5c-5047-b47d-705f224584f9" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288415 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =x,\\,t=\\frac{y-3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(\\frac{y-3}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=x$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25} & =x \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =25x \\\\ {(y-3)}^{2} & =25x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288417 13194139534441 true] [17592186288416 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288416 1041 "field-1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288416 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288417 13194139534441 true] [17592186288416 1110 #uuid "584ae79f-f0ff-5cc5-8c9c-d7676af6e402" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288417 1034 "3" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288417 1111 #uuid "c18fbe89-3cbf-5047-a7ca-2f741f7315c3" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288419 13194139534441 true] [17592186288418 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288418 1041 "field-2" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288418 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288419 13194139534441 true] [17592186288418 1110 #uuid "512da331-1f37-5611-b546-300d3b7ef138" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288419 1034 "25x" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288419 1111 #uuid "7cebe2d5-9118-5944-8a19-b830c1b4b248" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288421 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288423 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1089 "q-323229" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1100 "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola \n\n$$\nx-3=-{t}^{2},\\,y+4=-2t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(y\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1113 #uuid "9d85e680-26c7-5aac-9193-74809aef6804" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288420 1145 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =-(x-3),\\,t=-\\frac{y+4}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{y+4}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-(x-3)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4} & =-(x-3) \\\\ (y+4)^{2} & =-4(x-3) \\\\ {(y+4)}^{2} & =-4(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288421 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288422 13194139534441 true] [17592186288421 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288421 1041 "field-1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288421 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288422 13194139534441 true] [17592186288421 1110 #uuid "8f15f65c-b5da-5827-843f-3ab9389d9944" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288422 1034 "4" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288422 1111 #uuid "52ea6cc9-037b-5caf-8807-ba3a131db9ba" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288424 13194139534441 true] [17592186288423 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534441 true] [17592186288423 1041 "field-2" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288423 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288424 13194139534441 true] [17592186288423 1110 #uuid "6304e4eb-2a97-5376-8811-3dcf21cea22e" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288424 1034 "-4x+12" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288424 1111 #uuid "68c4bc08-c537-579b-bd5c-6f88aa96796f" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288426 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1089 "q-84822" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/6fcaa861fe507057f42c2194931bbc4a76d42891265ab40465832338cd8b5f4f.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1113 #uuid "d30c94fd-fa02-5be8-ad6f-2f4f9c02d497" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288425 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-4,-1),$ and passes through the point $(0,-3).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+4=2pt,\\,y+1=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(0,-3),$ we can substitute $x=0$ and $y=-3$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=2pt \\\\ -2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2pt \\\\ 2 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+4=2(-2)t,\\,y+1=(-2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-2{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288427 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288428 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288429 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288430 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288431 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1041 "selection" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288427 13194139534441 true] [17592186288426 1110 #uuid "da49ccce-4df5-5496-9bd2-9779aaf1a732" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288427 1034 "x+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-2{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288427 1111 #uuid "aaf02e36-db8b-556d-a1d9-932359ceef98" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288428 1034 "x+4=-4t,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288428 1111 #uuid "8a5b3f33-12a2-556c-b69c-8fc039817cc1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288429 1034 "x+4=-t,\\,y+1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288429 1111 #uuid "18666983-92bc-5d49-b058-32873deb7b00" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288430 1034 "x-4=-4t,\\,y-1=-2{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288430 1111 #uuid "118182d5-98b7-5d39-b306-f6fa747972e1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288431 1034 "x-4=-t,\\,y-1=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288431 1111 #uuid "a43d2dac-12b0-586a-918c-59c5a0986bc1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288433 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1089 "q-84824" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007650/assets/bb83d1803b8b81992b8ed3f93019088beaba6db0fccf7ab707f03c55ed308678.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1113 #uuid "c739ca25-5d75-5711-8097-97fe57c475b1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288432 1145 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(-1,2),$ and passes through the point $(-5,4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=2pt,\\,y-k=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nIn our case, $(h,k)=(-1,2),$ and so we have\n\n$$\nx+1=2pt,\\,y-2=p{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,4),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=4$ into the parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2pt \\\\ -2 & =pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(-\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+1=2(2)t,\\,y-2=(2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+1=4t,\\,y-2=2{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288434 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288435 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288436 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288437 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288438 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1041 "selection" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288437 13194139534441 true] [17592186288433 1110 #uuid "26302cf4-c209-56b7-bbed-7f797557ba1d" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288434 1034 "x+1=2t,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288434 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288434 1111 #uuid "d4742fad-09e4-509e-ad94-dee59336456e" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288435 1034 "x-1=4t,\\,y+2=2{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288435 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288435 1111 #uuid "219adf0c-dfc0-5f77-a8d8-4fb1806d2dd2" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288436 1034 "x+1=2t,\\,y-2=4{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288436 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288436 1111 #uuid "650a6ce7-9b00-530b-90ae-d297f7b59a93" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288437 1034 "x+1=4t,\\,y-2=2{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288437 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288437 1111 #uuid "4f7e0a0f-10e0-512f-a9ba-22366a5e9d97" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288438 1034 "x-1=2t,\\,y+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288438 1111 #uuid "c2a57fb0-cad7-5588-b8d3-d730ff66eb23" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288440 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1089 "q-84847" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1100 "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y-2)^{2}=16(x+6)?$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1113 #uuid "a45072fa-409b-5a6f-a637-083f290f0cb1" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288439 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-6,2).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx+6=p{t}^{2},\\,y-2=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =16(x+6) \\\\ 4p(x+6) & =16(x+6) \\\\ 4p & =16 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx+6=(4){t}^{2},\\,y-2=2(4)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx+6=4{t}^{2},\\,y-2=8t.\n$$" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288441 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288442 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288443 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288444 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288445 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1041 "selection" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288444 13194139534441 true] [17592186288440 1110 #uuid "da975536-095e-5181-8cb0-81f6b31aa0bc" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288441 1034 "x+6=2{t}^{2},\\,y-2=4t" 13194139534441 true] [17592186288441 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534441 true] [17592186288441 1111 #uuid "481f85f8-bfe2-5199-a60f-cd2e3b0130d5" 131941395344